<title>BELGIUM: Benelux bourses to sign cross-membership accord.</title>
<headline>Benelux bourses to sign cross-membership accord.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Benelux bourses -- Brussels, Amsterdam and Luxembourg -- were due to sign a memorandum of understanding on Friday aimed at linking their price and trading systems before European economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;The objective is to get this operational before the move to EMU...a maximum of 18 months,&quot; Brussels bourse chairman Olivier Lefebvre told Reuters.</p>
<p>The accord will effectively grant the bourses' brokerages and banks cross-membership. Lefebvre said a number of technical and legal issues still needed to be settled before the agreement could be finalised.</p>
<p>Representatives of the three exchanges are due to sign the agreement in Amsterdam at 1300 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
